WEBVTT

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.280
The circle entrance hours are between 07:30 and 09:00.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:41.030
<i>There's no way I'd go out with an otaku!</i>

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.000
Please take a look at the vendor timetable I handed out earlier.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.880
<i>I shouldn't be wasting time.</i>

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.090
We'll meet at 07:30 in
front of the Kokusai Tenjijou Station.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.480
What? Are we going to meet there?

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.890
Is that a problem?

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.180
Why don't we meet at the nearest station from
here and go together? It'll be more fun that way.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.050
It'll only be a hassle.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.530
If one person's late, everyone else will be, too.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.370
It'd be better to go separately.

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:12.220
I'll hand out the circle tickets today, too.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.630
You might have to go on ahead
of me
depending on the situation.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.430
Where's our booth located?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.280
Oh, I made photocopies.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.840
Is it the area you circled in red?

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.510
It's right in the middle of the island,

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.210
almost the same as last time.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.370
Well, that's to be expected.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:31.750
It'll be on day two, huh?

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:36.030
That reminds me, is the theme going to be Reass Mood?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.270
Well, it's not a problem if it is, right?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.030
What's the point of hiding it now?

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.560
We're going to find out one way or another!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.890
Well, it's a little unnecessary at this point in time.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.630
Well, I understand that much.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.750
I decided on a Kujiun Mugi x Sen book at the last minute.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:01.740
How should I say it? It's just how things turned out in the end.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:03.760
I see.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.690
Well, it's better to do what you're interested in.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.420
It's not that I'm interested in it.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.000
Never mind.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.640
How is the script coming along?

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.290
I can help out if you're not done.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:25.420
Only with the brushes and screen tones, though.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.390
I already gave it to the printer.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.630
In other words, I'm already finished.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:36.240
I was thinking about making a sample or a flyer of it by the day of the event.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.870
Wow, is that so?

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:40.380
That was quick.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.790
Maybe.

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.120
I received a discount for an early submission.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.320
Amazing.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.740
Then again, you were quick to finish when we
asked you to draw something last year, Ogiue-san.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.210
Not really.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:58.670
You don't have any other titles you're working on, do you?

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.340
You've already made photocopies, right?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.020
I did,

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.080
but you'll have to wait until it's made into a book.

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.900
Not again.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.930
You're such a shy girl!

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.730
Say whatever you want.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.660
Which printing company?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.320
Minami Printing,

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.400
the same place that Genshiken used last year.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.300
Oh, right.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:25.370
You didn't come along when
we went there last year, Ogiue-san.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:26.830
Did everything go smoothly?

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.740
More or less.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.740
I could have introduced you to them if you had asked me to.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.370
Sasahara-san, weren't you busy?

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.340
You can't afford to waste time.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.350
That's true.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:51.560
I just wanted a change of scenery.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.340
Ogiue-san's blunt, as always.

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.220
I wonder if she's being spiteful.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.900
It's not that I'm being spiteful.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.360
Is that so?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.280
Not at all.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.740
Then that's okay with me.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.490
Well, in any case, I'm looking forward to the book.

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.930
Ogiue-san's Mugi x Sen book, huh?

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.120
I can't wait to read it. Right, Sasahara-san?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:15.930
Yeah.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.710
You aren't allowed to read it, Sasahara-san.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.290
Why not?

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.470
I'd rather not explain every small detail.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:26.630
No woman would be happy if a man saw something like that.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.170
You definitely aren't allowed to read it.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.630
I understand how you feel about it,

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.870
but he's helping you out.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.270
That's okay.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:37.660
It isn't a problem.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:41.270
Everyone has something they don't want others to see.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.170
I think this is a little different.

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.400
Oh, really?

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.920
You're right, though.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:49.320
I'm sorry.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:50.520
It's okay.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:58.960
That's it! If you have something that isn't yaoi,
why don't you ask Sasahara-san to take a look at it?

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:04.550
You let me look at some sketches for submission purposes,

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.760
which means you're also drawing original work, right?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.380
Fortunately for you,
Sasahara-san's trying to become a manga editor,

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.380
so he might be able to give you some advice.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.400
No, that's a little too much.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.780
It's better to hear an objective opinion
rather than trusting your own intuition.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.610
Isn't a man's opinion invaluable to you?

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:33.590
Well, that's true,

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.750
but it's not like I want to
become a professional.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.340
I don't think that's necessary.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.960
I'm just a student who hasn't even secured a job.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:51.090
That aside, I've been reminded of my own shortcomings lately.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.340
I don't even think I'll be hired anytime soon.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:58.480
Impersonating an editor and commenting on something would just be too pathetic.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.190
That's true.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:03.650
They're mostly yaoi titles anyway.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:05.050
Yeah.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.220
We'll stop by again.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.410
As long as you're not here for weird reasons.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.250
Sorry for making you come when you're so busy.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:20.460
I guess you're right.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.290
I didn't mean that in a sarcastic way.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.960
It's not a big deal.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.300
I wanted to do something like this a bit more.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.800
You wouldn't understand.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:46.270
<i>There's no doubt that Sasahara-san and Ogiue-san
know how they feel about each other.</i>

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:47.920
There's no way...

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.240
<i>I wonder why she hates otakus that much.</i>

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.250
That's why I hate myself, too!

00:07:55.560 --> 00:08:00.650
Will you really be able to express your embarrassing
delusions in a book that the whole world will be able to see?

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.060
<i>The fact that she can't show it to him
means she has trouble expressing herself.</i>

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.050
<i>Not being able to express yourself is terrible.</i>

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.640
<i>In my case, I was fortunate to have Tanaka-san.</i>

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.020
<i>It took a while for us, too.</i>

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:29.030
<i>I wonder if they just need a little more time,</i>

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:33.990
<i>especially since this person seems a lot weaker than Tanaka-san.</i>

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:38.750
<i>If he could muster the courage to say that
he likes Ogiue-san, she'd definitely accept him.</i>

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.570
Aren't you looking forward to the Comifes?

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.120
Oh, yeah.

00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:52.370
<i>Nothing will happen unless you say it clearly.</i>

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:53.440
<i>That's for sure.</i>

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.450
<i>Nobody's coming.</i>

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.430
<i>Sasahara's busy looking for a job,</i>

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:16.410
<i>and Ogiue-san's probably busy preparing for the Comifes.</i>

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:21.040
<i>Ohno-san and Tanaka are probably making cosplay costumes,</i>

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.460
<i>and who knows what Kuchiki-kun's doing.</i>

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:31.270
<i>Kasukabe-san must be over her head with work,
and Kousaka's working as an ero-game developer.</i>

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.070
What's going to happen at the next Comifes?

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.260
It's open.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:48.850
Hello?

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:52.230
Hello.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.170
Oh, you must be Madarame,

00:09:56.170 --> 00:09:57.650
just like Kanako said.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:00.550
Massive glasses, thin neck, tall.

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:02.910
You're a typical souuke.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.460
<i>She came in! She came in!
W-W-W-W-What should I do?</i>

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.670
Oh, yes. Real Madarame.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.900
You're so shy. How do you like a greeting like this?

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:27.170
You don't do this in Japan, do you?

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.560
Angela!

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.450
I told you not to walk around alone!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.480
Sorry, Kanako,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.940
but I wanted to see the clubroom first.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.990
I'm introducing you.

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.550
Ohno-san, huh?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.580
<i>What incredible hair!</i>

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.950
Are you stupid?

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.590
Sue!

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.090
You can't say that to anyone.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:03.720
It's only lucky Madarame-san understands parodies.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.180
Many people don't.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.670
They'd hit you for that!

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.890
Bunch of idiots!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.230
What?

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.870
That kind of line really suits you, Suzy!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:14.880
Angela, don't encourage her.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.930
Why not? We're in Japan.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:20.520
Just don't.
Many people wouldn't
understand it, even here in Japan.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:20.950
<i>This is stressful.
Just don't.
Many people wouldn't
understand it, even here in Japan.</i>

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:22.150
They don't?
<i>This is stressful.</i>

00:11:23.940 --> 00:11:26.620
It might be a little too late for introductions,

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:30.300
but these are my friends from America.
Angela Burton...

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:31.210
Hi!

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:33.130
...and Susanna Hopkins.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.350
Please call her Sue or Suzy.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.700
They suddenly came because
they wanted to attend the Comifes.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:43.330
It was really sudden.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:47.550
They called me in the morning
and asked me to pick them up at Narita.

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:49.490
Wow, that's pretty self-centered.

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.480
Come on, I've got to see your boyfriend.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.080
I want to have my costume made!

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:56.360
You should have told me before, though.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:58.200
He can't make it so quickly.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.170
That's why...

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.620
I'm sorry to say I can't be a vendor.

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.130
Can you two handle it by yourselves?

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.580
I'm really sorry.

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:14.160
Well, we'll manage.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.950
One way or another.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.990
Oh, I just remembered I have to work on Saturday.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:23.950
And you're going to get all the doujinshi, aren't you, Sue?

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:34.360
Yeah, it'll be pretty tough at this point in time.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.030
Of course it will.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.760
He says he can't. You're too late.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:39.820
Oh.

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:42.030
Which character did you want to do?

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.600
Can I do this one?

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.550
Oh, this one, huh?

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:52.460
It's pretty skimpy, but I still need to get the materials.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.080
If you don't think you can do it, you have to tell them properly.

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:00.400
Well, yeah.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.510
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.640
Souichirou, please.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.460
Your untidy beard is nice.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:14.730
Ouch!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.280
You got so violent, Kanako!

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:21.350
That's because I didn't have a
boyfriend when I was in the States!

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.330
In any case, I'll give it a shot.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.370
If I can't do it, pretend this conversation never happened.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.020
Are you sure?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.330
You're too honest.

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:37.260
Great! Thank you, Souichirou!

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:38.750
It's nothing.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.100
Do you want to measure me then?

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.400
Do you want to take her measurements?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.930
Oh, I see. I think I should let you do the honors, Ohno-s—

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.650
Make it, fools!

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:57.030
Angela, put on your clothes now!
Come on!

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:57.410
Why are you staying that way, Angela?

00:13:57.410 --> 00:13:58.970
So cute.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.410
That's how it is.

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:09.190
You better not flirt with him.
Japanese men would take it seriously.

00:14:09.190 --> 00:14:12.710
They would? I'm not saying "I love you" or anything.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:15.810
We Japanese believe in non-verbal communication

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:18.550
and try to understand unsaid feelings.

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:21.490
It sometimes brings whimsical speculation.

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:22.900
It does?

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:25.290
And that happens only to otaku?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.880
I think not.

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:32.060
Oh, that's why butlers understand
our feelings and take care of us so well.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.230
Welcome back, master.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:37.870
That's a maid!

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:41.400
I can't wait to go to the butlers' cafe!

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.540
Yo!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:11.260
You're so funny. I can't believe you're souuke!

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.450
Hey.

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:16.730
Kanako, coming soon.

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:22.600
Ohno-san... coming soon.
She'll be here any moment, huh?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.810
Um, that's... okay!

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.100
Wait, should I have said "all right"

00:15:28.140 --> 00:15:29.490
or just "yes"?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.240
Hey.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:34.830
Do you have the last issue?
Can I borrow the August issue?

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:38.670
What? That's Reass Mood.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.880
August. August.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:44.340
Oh, do you want to see the August issue?

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.570
August means August, huh?

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.060
The previous issue, huh?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.910
Let's see.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:55.820
Is this it?

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.760
Oh, that's it!

00:15:58.450 --> 00:15:59.980
Thanks, Madarame-san.

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:02.460
Oh, it's nothing...

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.240
You're welcome.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:07.180
Oh, good.

00:16:09.730 --> 00:16:10.830
Hey.

00:16:14.590 --> 00:16:15.860
Me? There?

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:16.460
You want me to come over there?

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.730
Yes.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:22.890
I don't know what I should do.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.010
Oh, I see.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.650
Oh.

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.900
You're so sensible. Japanese people are great.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:29.150
Sorry, I was testing you because Kanako
told me that Japanese men are so sensible.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:33.230
It's true. Butlers at the cafe did everything for me,

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:35.570
and most of them wore glasses.

00:17:36.510 --> 00:17:39.360
Only they're trying too hard.

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:42.430
They show too much of themselves trying to be sensible.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:45.130
Do they want to show how sensible they are?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:48.160
Well, sensibility is not enough for me.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:02.180
Your fingers are perfect.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.810
They're so thin and long.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.220
Your finger, beautiful.

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.100
Hey.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.630
It sounds like someone's inside.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:42.020
Yeah.

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:44.440
You're here, just as I thought.

00:18:45.500 --> 00:18:49.400
Hello, nice to see you! I've heard about you from Kanako.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.110
You must be Angela. I'm Saki Kasukabe.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:56.540
Oh, I've heard about you, too, and I feel like I know you well.

00:18:56.540 --> 00:18:58.830
Kanako's talking about you all the time.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.410
Nice to see you, I'm Angela.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.830
How do you do, Angela-san? I'm Kousaka Makoto.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:10.260
Oh, hello, I'm Angela.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:15.150
How do you know Kanako?

00:19:15.150 --> 00:19:19.190
Well, she was my neighbor,
but we didn't know each other at first.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:22.890
<i>Will she answer in Japanese if someone speaks to her like that?</i>

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:28.020
And then, suddenly, she started to stay alone.

00:19:28.020 --> 00:19:30.670
Oh, this story is going to be serious?

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:35.730
No. And one day, Sue was doing the Sailor Moon.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.530
What's Sailor Moon?

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.580
Oh, Saki-san.

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.380
We were just talking.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:45.440
Oh, nice to see you, Suzy. I'm Saki Kasukabe.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.550
You have an arrogant attitude for a Nobita-like character!

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:07.150
Even I know that!

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:12.310
No, Sue, don't.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.530
That was really funny!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:23.240
Sue, you're great.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.170
Are you stupid?

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:26.850
Not again.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:36.040
Japanese people are really sensible,

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.890
What? Yeah, yes.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:42.220
but we understand people, too, naturally.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.540
Still...

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.350
We must say something to be understood.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:56.880
I don't understand what you're talking about.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.100
Well,

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.870
I'm not telling you.

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:45.920
Keroro is the strongest animal character.

00:22:45.920 --> 00:22:47.660
Don't you understand?

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:49.780
No, I don't understand at all.

00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:53.730
But not stronger than Retsu and Gou.

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:56.020
That you said before.

00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:09.560
What's wrong with him?

00:23:10.780 --> 00:23:13.920
I-Is your family r-rich, Kousaka?

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.630
My dad's an ordinary businessman.

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:16.680
Why do you ask?

00:23:16.680 --> 00:23:20.420
Y-You buy a lot of games and D-DVDs,

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.460
s-so I thought you had a lot of money.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:25.470
It's probably because I don't spend much on other things.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.860
I don't mind skipping meals.

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:30.270
Y-You mean you're perfectly okay
with food from the convenience store?

00:23:30.270 --> 00:23:31.920
I'm not too fond of it.

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:36.450
I'd rather not waste money and
time on things like sleep and food.

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:37.400
I'm not interested in those kinds of things.

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:39.990
I-Is it really a matter of whether you're interested?
